  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="5c4d70dc-e487-45ef-b54c-4b2011eccc9d"><problem><para>
      <para>The expression \(9t + 7.25\) represents the cost to purchase tickets for a concert, where \(t\) is the number of tickets. A group of friends paid $79.25 for tickets. How many tickets were bought?</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>6 tickets</para><para>8 tickets</para><para>10 tickets</para><para>12 tickets</para></problem><solution><para>8 tickets</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is 8 tickets. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
